/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 71 0 R
/T (Project Inclusion is a digital health and community empowerment initiative designed to improve access to physiotherapy, wellness, and inclusive care for underserved populations in Rwanda. With a focus on musculoskeletal \(MSK\) conditions With a focus on musculoskeletal \(MSK\) conditions and disability-friendly health services, the program empowers community health workers \(CHWs\), caregivers, and individuals with disabilities through technology-enhanced tools and locally adaptable educational content.)
/E (Project Inclusion is a digital health and community empowerment initiative designed to improve access to physiotherapy, wellness, and inclusive care for underserved populations in Rwanda. With a focus on musculoskeletal \(MSK\) conditions With a focus on musculoskeletal \(MSK\) conditions and disability-friendly health services, the program empowers community health workers \(CHWs\), caregivers, and individuals with disabilities through technology-enhanced tools and locally adaptable educational content.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 71 0 R
/T ( It was launched in 2021 by Physiotools Oy \(a subsidiary of Physitrack PLC\), in partnership with JAMK University of Applied Sciences and local universities in Indonesia and Rwanda and the Inclusion App was developed. )
/E ( It was launched in 2021 by Physiotools Oy \(a subsidiary of Physitrack PLC\), in partnership with JAMK University of Applied Sciences and local universities in Indonesia and Rwanda and the Inclusion App was developed. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 71 0 R
/T (It empowers Community Health Workers \(CHWs\) to deliver basic, safe and effective rehabilitation services directly within communities. With over 15,000 people already supported and 90% reporting recovery without needing further referral, the Inclusion App has proven to be 18 times more cost-effective than traditional facility-based rehabilitation. In 2025, the Project Inclusion transitioned to a new independent entity: Lumira Link, dedicated to scaling the initiative across ecosystems and countries.)
/E (It empowers Community Health Workers \(CHWs\) to deliver basic, safe and effective rehabilitation services directly within communities. With over 15,000 people already supported and 90% reporting recovery without needing further referral, the Inclusion App has proven to be 18 times more cost-effective than traditional facility-based rehabilitation. In 2025, the Project Inclusion transitioned to a new independent entity: Lumira Link, dedicated to scaling the initiative across ecosystems and countries.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 71 0 R
/T (This concept seeks funding to scale the Inclusion App across 14 additional districts, training 930 CHWs through a two-day orientation, distributing pre-installed smartphones, and providing ongoing monthly field supervision and refresher training. The intervention will enable the delivery of over 244,000 personalized exercise programs annually, transforming access to care for thousands of people living in remote areas.)
/E (This concept seeks funding to scale the Inclusion App across 14 additional districts, training 930 CHWs through a two-day orientation, distributing pre-installed smartphones, and providing ongoing monthly field supervision and refresher training. The intervention will enable the delivery of over 244,000 personalized exercise programs annually, transforming access to care for thousands of people living in remote areas.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
