141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 72 0 R
/T (Over 2.4 billion people worldwide currently need rehabilitation services. In Rwanda, the need is growing rapidly, driven by the increasing burden of non-communicable diseases \(NCDs\), aging and chronic conditions. Despite this, fewer than 500 Physiotherapists are tasked with serving a population of over 14 million. This imbalance is even more pronounced at the community level, where over 90% of Rwandans access care through primary healthcare facilities, yet rehabilitation professionals are only available at secondary and tertiary levels, and in limited numbers.)
/E (Over 2.4 billion people worldwide currently need rehabilitation services. In Rwanda, the need is growing rapidly, driven by the increasing burden of non-communicable diseases \(NCDs\), aging and chronic conditions. Despite this, fewer than 500 Physiotherapists are tasked with serving a population of over 14 million. This imbalance is even more pronounced at the community level, where over 90% of Rwandans access care through primary healthcare facilities, yet rehabilitation professionals are only available at secondary and tertiary levels, and in limited numbers.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 72 0 R
/T (The forecasted global rise in rehabilitation needs will not leave Rwanda untouched. As people live longer, but with more chronic conditions and disabilities, the gap between demand and service availability widens. This challenge threatens the Universal Health Coverage \(UHC\) goal, especially for underserved populations. Without accessible and affordable rehabilitation, rural communities are left behind.)
/E (The forecasted global rise in rehabilitation needs will not leave Rwanda untouched. As people live longer, but with more chronic conditions and disabilities, the gap between demand and service availability widens. This challenge threatens the Universal Health Coverage \(UHC\) goal, especially for underserved populations. Without accessible and affordable rehabilitation, rural communities are left behind.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
