188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (Following ethical clearance from the National Ethics Committee, we are set to scale the Inclusion App across 14 additional districts \(Nyabihu, Gicumbi, Karongi, Nyamasheke, Nyamagabe, Nyaruguru, Huye, Gisagara, Nyanza, Ruhango, Kicukiro, Bugesera, Rwamagana, Kayonza\), adding to our existing implementation in Musanze, Burera, and Nyarugenge districts. We will select one health centre with maximum population in their catchment area and train 66 community health workers on use of digital technologies in providing rehabilitation services. Under two days orientation training, a total of 930 community health workers will be trained in seven clusters, with one cluster made of 130 CHWs and equipped with smartphones with already installed Inclusion App.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E ( Inclusion App provides in app short video instructions for each contextualized exercise that was pre-designed by rehabilitation experts for the most prevalent cases in Rwanda such as low back pain, knee pain, elbow pain, hip pain, shoulder pain, neck pain, geriatric exercises, and general well-being exercises. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
