/P 81 0 R
/E (. By equipping Community Health Workers with digital tools to deliver essential rehabilitation services at the grassroots level, the project not only addresses critical health inequities and contributes to SDG 3 \(Good Health and Well-being\) and SDG 10 \(Reduced Inequalities\), but also significantly reduces financial strain on vulnerable households, directly contributing to SDG 1 \(No Poverty\). )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (By restoring mobility and functional independence, it enables individuals to return to productive activities and livelihoods, fostering decent work and economic growth at the community level \(SDG 8\). )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (This digital-first, but not digital-only, model strengthens Rwanda's primary healthcare system by building a sustainable, functional, and effective community health workforce, demonstrating the power of digital connectivity for tangible, long-term impact. Supporting the scale-up of the Lumiralink App will amplify the impact on Rwandan communities, foster health equity, and showcase the strong bilateral cooperation between China and Rwanda in advancing inclusive digital health innovation.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
