/Title (It empowers Community Health Workers \(CHWs\) to deliver basic, safe and effective rehabilitation services directly within communities. With over 15,000 people already supported and 90% reporting recovery without needing further referral, the Inclusion App has proven to be 18 times more cost-effective than traditional facility-based rehabilitation. In 2025, the Project Inclusion transitioned to a new independent entity: Lumira Link, dedicated to scaling the initiative across ecosystems and countries.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 501 0 R
/Prev 789 0 R
/Next 790 0 R
>>
endobj
882 0 obj
<<
/Title (The forecasted global rise in rehabilitation needs will not leave Rwanda untouched. As people live longer, but with more chronic conditions and disabilities, the gap between demand and service availability widens. This challenge threatens the Universal Health Coverage \(UHC\) goal, especially for underserved populations. Without accessible and affordable rehabilitation, rural communities are left behind.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 685 0 R
/Prev 791 0 R
/Next 792 0 R
